//! The fs subsystem's code (seed-core-design §2c.3): everything of the
//! subsystem that is neither `unsafe.rs` nor `types.rs`, in one file.
//!
//! Sections follow the order of the old module declarations; each banner
//! names the topic file it was (`bio` was bio.rs) and the file's module
//! doc follows it as the section's header comment. Inside a section the
//! items keep their original order. Type definitions are in `types.rs`,
//! the audited unsafe edges in `unsafe.rs`; the unsafe that is still
//! scattered over the sections is collected in pass 3.
//!
//! The old files each carried `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` (13 of them:
//! dev_t.rs, fdreap.rs, file_hooks.rs, io_completion.rs, leaf_glue.rs,
//! lock_hooks.rs, locks.rs, mount_table.rs, notify_events.rs,
//! notify_hooks.rs, path.rs, perf_ctr.rs, readahead.rs). A merged file
//! cannot carry it per section and the sections still hold unsafe, so the
//! attribute is dropped here; it comes back with pass 3, when the last
//! scattered unsafe block has moved to `unsafe.rs` and the whole file can
//! carry it again.
//!
//! Dropped with them: `#![allow(clippy::missing_safety_doc)]` of pidfd.rs —
//! it allows a clippy lint that nothing in the tree turns on, so it has no
//! effect to preserve.
//!
//! The file's NAME overstates until the shrink stage has run: it holds all
//! of the subsystem's code under the hot-path name, not a verified set of
//! hot-path functions (§2c.3, user decision 2026-11-25).

